-- title:
--   Two maximal quaternion orders simultaneously standard at a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, each assumed to be a maximal order in the sense that it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is not properly contained in any submodule with these four properties. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $\ell$ be a prime number with $\ell\in v$, and let $\varphi$ be a ring isomorphism $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v\cong M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ with $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for all $r\in\mathbb{Q}_v$. The assertion is that there is an $e\in\mathbb{N}$ with the following two properties. First, there is $h\in GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ such that, for $x$ in the tensor product, $x$ lies in the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ exactly when $h^{-1}\varphi(x)h$ has all entries in that valuation ring, while the corresponding subgroup attached to $\Lambda_2$ consists of those $x$ for which $d^{-1}h^{-1}\varphi(x)h\,d$ has integral entries, where $d=\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell^{e})$. Second, the same statement holds with the roles of $\Lambda_1$ and $\Lambda_2$ interchanged, for some (possibly different) $h\in GL_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ and the same $e$.
--
--   This is the local elementary-divisor normalisation of a pair of maximal orders at a place where the quaternion algebra splits: both completed lattices can be put simultaneously into the standard position $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_v)$ and $d\,M_2(\mathbb{Z}_v)\,d^{-1}$ with $d=\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell^{e})$, symmetrically in the two orders. It supplies the split-place input for the local index computations showing that the Eichler order $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ has equal index in $\Lambda_1$ and in $\Lambda_2$, and is used by the statements about Eichler orders of squarefree level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsMaximalOrder_exists_pair_localBox_iff_conj_diagonal_pow_mem_adicCompletionIntegers.lean

